WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.540
This is the Strategya Catalog.

2
00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:03.820
Here's how to read it,

3
00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:05.030
card by card.

4
00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:07.500
Strategies come in three tiers,

5
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.040
entry, intermediate, and expert.

6
00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:11.950
Each tier includes the ones below it,

7
00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:13.890
so expert has everything.

8
00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:16.320
Every card opens with today's position.

9
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.190
Here is the same Bitcoin card

10
00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:19.930
on two days of our example.

11
00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:23.490
On October 12th, it was 100% in Bitcoin.

12
00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:27.160
On October 26th, it is 100% in cash.

13
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.440
A card can also be long or short,

14
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:30.620
like this one.

15
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:33.650
Long plus short strategies are in early access.

16
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:35.970
Their results are still preliminary.

17
00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.830
Below the position, whether it changed today

18
00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:41.270
and the last change with its date.

19
00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.210
Here, from Bitcoin to cash,

20
00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:44.640
13 days ago.

21
00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.430
Then, the last trade,

22
00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:48.370
its result, how long it lasted,

23
00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:50.240
and the price it closed at.

24
00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:53.690
On rotation strategies, which move between several assets,

25
00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:55.380
you will see cash-to-cash,

26
00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.240
the result of the whole stay in

27
00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.880
the market across every asset it held.

28
00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:03.510
This rotation card was in SUI on October 12th.

29
00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.630
By October 26th, it was back in cash.

30
00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:08.900
Its whole stay in the market,

31
00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:13.360
cash-to-cash, made 61.44% in 110 days

32
00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:16.370
across 11 trades in this backtest.

33
00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:18.660
On the right, the live price.

34
00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:20.000
Tap price chart.

35
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.150
The chart shows the daily closes of the asset,

36
00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:25.380
orange while the strategy held it,

37
00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:27.150
green while it sat in cash.

38
00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:28.910
You can choose the window,

39
00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:30.250
six months, one year,

40
00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:32.590
two years, or since 2023.

41
00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:34.960
The line at the bottom tells you how the

42
00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.320
asset did over that window and how much of

43
00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.680
the time the strategy was in position.

44
00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.240
Now tap plus to open the full card.

45
00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:45.840
First, the strategy against simply holding the asset.

46
00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.810
Same $1,000, same start date.

47
00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:52.790
The strategy turned it into $6,768,

48
00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:56.510
holding Bitcoin into $4,852.

49
00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:59.590
The multiplier says the same thing in one number,

50
00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:02.310
6.8 times against 4.9.

51
00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:05.600
Max drawdown is the worst drop along the way,

52
00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.530
13% for the strategy,

53
00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.110
49% for holding.

54
00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:11.790
This number matters as much as the return.

55
00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:14.000
There is an old rule in trading.

56
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.840
It is not how much you make,

57
00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.280
it is how much you do not lose.

58
00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.790
Capital you keep is capital that keeps compounding.

59
00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:24.250
CAGR is the average yearly growth,

60
00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:27.650
and MAR divides that growth by the drawdown.

61
00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:29.350
Return per unit of pain.

62
00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:30.670
Higher is better.

63
00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:33.700
In this backtest, the strategy beats simply

64
00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:36.100
holding on every one of these numbers.

65
00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.790
More return, a much smaller

66
00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.710
drawdown and a higher MAR.

67
00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:42.360
That comparison is what the card is for.

68
00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.270
Look at the green line.

69
00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:45.630
Where it goes flat,

70
00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:49.220
the strategy was in cash while holding kept falling.

71
00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:51.150
That flat stretch is the protection.

72
00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:52.910
You can switch the window up

73
00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:54.640
here and read the longer,

74
00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:58.000
harder stretch since 2018 just below.

75
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.960
Watch the numbers move as you change the window.

76
00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:02.340
Two years, one year,

77
00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:03.280
six months.

78
00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.720
The short windows show how

79
00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.700
the rule has done lately.

80
00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:10.000
Tap any info icon for a plain English definition.

81
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.990
Next, the position history,

82
00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:13.470
a ribbon of every day.

83
00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:15.320
Orange when it held Bitcoin,

84
00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.230
green when it was in cash.

85
00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.170
Tap a band to read that trade.

86
00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:20.820
Open the replay to watch

87
00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:22.560
the backtest bar by bar.

88
00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.840
Press play and let it run for a moment.

89
00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:26.230
Green is the strategy.

90
00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:29.110
Orange is holding, both from $1,000.

91
00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:31.160
You can step through at one,

92
00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:32.780
five, or 20 times speed,

93
00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:34.620
and the line above tells you what

94
00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:36.240
the card said on that day.

95
00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:39.000
At 20 times, the whole backtest

96
00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.190
runs to the end in seconds.

97
00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:42.880
The gap between the two lines is

98
00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:45.590
what the rule made in this simulation.

99
00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:47.270
Open the trade history,

100
00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:49.200
every trade on one line.

101
00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.920
When it bought, when it sold,

102
00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:53.300
at what prices, and what it returned.

103
00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.630
The cash stretches are listed too,

104
00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:58.060
so you can see how long the rule waited.

105
00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:00.880
Then the statistics, like a strategy tester.

106
00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:04.640
Total P&L, everything the strategy made over the window.

107
00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.560
Year to date, win rate,

108
00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.780
how many trades closed with a gain,

109
00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:12.520
profit factor, dollars won for every dollar lost,

110
00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:15.410
average monthly return, average holding time,

111
00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:18.240
and the typical winner against the typical loser.

112
00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:19.960
Each number has its own window

113
00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:22.090
selector and its own info icon.

114
00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:25.710
Switch the window and every number updates with it.

115
00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:26.870
Tap an info icon and its

116
00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:30.670
plain English definition appears right below.

117
00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:31.840
And at the bottom,

118
00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:33.720
every month and every year.

119
00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:34.950
Green for a gain,

120
00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:36.160
red for a loss,

121
00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.320
and the year's total on the right.

122
00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:40.250
A gray zero means it stayed

123
00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:42.240
in cash the whole month.

124
00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.950
Cards update every day after the close.

125
00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:47.420
Midnight UTC for crypto after

126
00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.940
the NYSE close for stocks.

127
00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:52.110
Everything here is a simulated backtest,

128
00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:55.560
not real performance, and not investment advice.

